codex
Tracing shows the boundary discrepancy clearly: pydantic-core’s Python serializer merges extras after fields (overwriting the dict value), while its JSON serializer emits duplicate object keys (`{"x":1,"x":2}`), whose last value wins when parsed. The same defect recurs inside nested models and lists, so a top-level-only dict patch would be insufficient; I’m checking the upstream architecture and available serializer controls for a recursive, contract-preserving fix.
