{"body":"### Initial Checks\n\n- [x] I confirm that I'm using Pydantic V2\n\n### Description\n\nWhen a model uses extra='allow' and a field has an alias, providing both an alias key and its corresponding field-name key in the input leads to inconsistent serialization. The alias value is used as the declared field value, while the field-name value remains in model_extra. During serialization, the extra entry collides with the declared field's output key. As a result:\n\n  - model_dump() overwrites the validated field value with the extra value\n  - model_dump_json() emits both values under the field-name key\n\nExpected behavior: serialization would not overwrite the resolved field value with extra data\n\n### Example Code\n\n```Python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field\n\n\nclass Model(BaseModel):\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra='allow')\n    x: int = Field(alias='X')\n\n\npayload = {'X': 1, 'x': 2}\nmodel = Model.model_validate(payload)\n\nprint('field value:', model.x)\nprint('extra:', model.model_extra)\nprint('model_dump():', model.model_dump())\nprint('model_dump_json():', model.model_dump_json())\n```\n\n### Python, Pydantic & OS Version\n\n```Text\npydantic version: 2.12.5\n        pydantic-core version: 2.41.5\n          pydantic-core build: profile=release pgo=false\n               python version: 3.12.12 (main, Feb 12 2026, 00:42:14) [Clang 21.1.4 ]\n                     platform: Linux-6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2-x86_64-with-glibc2.35\n             related packages: typing_extensions-4.15.0\n                       commit: unknown\n```","closedByPullRequestsReferences":[],"comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM7tYKQ9","author":{"login":"yangbaechu"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"This issue seems to point to shared serialization logic, not just the `BaseModel` dump entrypoints (for example, `model_construct()`, `TypedDict`, and pydantic dataclasses). The shared fields serialization path seems to assume there are no duplicate keys, which is relevant to the current overwrite / duplicate-output behavior.\n\nA possible direction might be to track resolved output keys in the shared serialization layer, likely around `GeneralFieldsSerializer.serialize_iterators()`, and then skip extra entries that would serialize to the same key as a declared field. That would improve consistency in both Python and JSON serialization anywhere the same shared serialization path is involved, without changing validation behavior. Does that direction sound reasonable?","createdAt":"2026-03-02T07:03:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12884#issuecomment-3982533693","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM7tclc8","author":{"login":"Viicos"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The repr of the model (`Model(x=1, x=2)`) is also a bit weird. I think it would make sense to align the JSON output to the Python one, but this can't happen in v2.","createdAt":"2026-03-02T11:06:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12884#issuecomment-3983693628","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM7x-SRu","author":{"login":"AhsanSheraz"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hey @Viicos & @yangbaechu \nI've looked into this and the root cause is in `GeneralFieldsSerializer.serialize_iterators()` — when processing `__pydantic_extra__` entries, there was no check for key collisions with already-serialized field output keys. This caused declared field values to be overwritten in `model_dump()` and duplicate keys in `model_dump_json()`.\n\nOpened a fix here: #12918","createdAt":"2026-03-14T05:37:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"low-quality","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12884#issuecomment-4059636846","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM7yBOkR","author":{"login":"AhsanSheraz"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"> Hey [@Viicos](https://github.com/Viicos) & [@yangbaechu](https://github.com/yangbaechu) I've looked into this and the root cause is in `GeneralFieldsSerializer.serialize_iterators()` — when processing `__pydantic_extra__` entries, there was no check for key collisions with already-serialized field output keys. This caused declared field values to be overwritten in `model_dump()` and duplicate keys in `model_dump_json()`.\n> \n> Opened a fix here: [#12918](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/pull/12918)\n\nHey @Viicos can you share what was wrong with the solution and what you are expecting for the fix?","createdAt":"2026-03-14T11:53:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"low-quality","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12884#issuecomment-4060408081","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM8AAAABN47z4w","author":{"login":"thatssoheil"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Reproduced on current main (v2.14.0b1, pydantic-core 2.48.0):\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field\n\nclass Model(BaseModel):\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra='allow')\n    x: int = Field(alias='X')\n\npayload = {'X': 1, 'x': 2}\nmodel = Model.model_validate(payload)\n\nprint('field value:', model.x)          # 1\nprint('extra:', model.model_extra)      # {'x': 2}\nprint('model_dump():', model.model_dump())          # {'x': 2}  <- wrong, overwrites validated value\nprint('model_dump_json():', model.model_dump_json()) # {\"x\":1,\"x\":2} <- duplicate key\n```\n\nBoth failure modes from the report confirmed: `model_dump()` lets the extra value overwrite the resolved field value, and `model_dump_json()` emits both values under the same key.\n\nI'd like to work on this. Plan: in the serializer, when a field with an alias (or any field whose output key can collide with an extra key) is being serialized, skip the colliding key from `model_extra` so the validated field value wins, and add a regression test covering `model_dump()` + `model_dump_json()` for the alias-collision case.\n\nCould I be assigned to this issue?\n","createdAt":"2026-08-08T16:49:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12884#issuecomment-5227082723","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"number":12884,"state":"OPEN","title":"extra='allow' can let alias/name collisions overwrite validated field output during serialization","url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12884"}

