{"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #12884\n\nWhen a model uses `extra='allow'` and a field has an alias, providing both the alias key and the field-name key in input causes serialization issues:\n- `model_dump()` overwrites the declared field value with the extra value\n- `model_dump_json()` emits duplicate keys\n\n### Root Cause\n\nIn `GeneralFieldsSerializer.serialize_iterators()`, the extras iterator (`__pydantic_extra__`) processes entries without checking whether their keys collide with already-serialized field output keys.\n\n### Fix\n\nTrack the output keys of fields that were actually serialized during the main dict iteration. When processing extras, skip any entry whose key matches an already-serialized field output key. This correctly handles:\n\n- Field name vs alias collisions\n- `serialization_alias` collisions with `by_alias=True`\n- `by_alias=True` where alias differs from extra key (no false skips)\n- Schema-excluded fields (their output keys are not tracked, so extras with the same name still appear)\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`pydantic-core/src/serializers/fields.rs`**: Added `AHashSet<String>` to collect serialized field output keys during main iteration, then skip colliding extras\n- **`tests/test_serialize.py`**: Added 7 regression tests covering `model_dump`, `model_dump_json`, `by_alias`, `serialization_alias`, multiple fields, and excluded fields\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] Existing `test_model_allow_extra` passes (previously failed with over-aggressive approach)\n- [x] All 96 serialization tests pass\n- [x] All 471 extra-related tests pass\n- [x] All 838 alias-related tests pass\n- [x] Lint checks pass (`ruff check` + `ruff format --check`)\n- [x] Rust compiles cleanly with no warnings (`cargo check`)","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM7x-BgP","author":{"login":"codspeed"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<!-- __CODSPEED_PERFORMANCE_REPORT_COMMENT__ -->\n## Merging this PR will **not alter performance**\n\n\n\n\n`✅ 212` untouched benchmarks  \n\n\n\n---\n\n<sub>Comparing <code>AhsanSheraz:fix/extra-allow-alias-serialization-collision</code> (a95f578) with <code>main</code> (f2bc256)</sub>\n\n<a href=\"https://codspeed.io/pydantic/pydantic/branches/AhsanSheraz%3Afix%2Fextra-allow-alias-serialization-collision?utm_source=github&utm_medium=comment-v2&utm_content=button\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://codspeed.io/pr-report/open-in-codspeed-dark.svg\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://codspeed.io/pr-report/open-in-codspeed-light.svg\">\n    <img alt=\"Open in CodSpeed\" src=\"https://codspeed.io/pr-report/open-in-codspeed-light.svg\" width=\"169\" height=\"32\">\n  </picture>\n</a>\n\n","createdAt":"2026-03-14T05:07:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/pull/12918#issuecomment-4059568143","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOBWBCuM7x-P09","author":{"login":"github-actions"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Coverage report\n\n\n<img title=\"Coverage for the whole project is 96%. Previous coverage rate is not available, cannot report on evolution.\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Coverage-96%25-orange.svg\"> <img title=\"100% of the statement lines added by this PR are covered\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/PR%20Coverage-100%25-brightgreen.svg\">\n\n_This PR does not seem to contain any modification to coverable code._\n\n<!-- This comment was produced by python-coverage-comment-action -->","createdAt":"2026-03-14T05:29:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/pull/12918#issuecomment-4059626813","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"files":[{"path":"pydantic-core/src/serializers/fields.rs","additions":9,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tests/test_serialize.py","additions":104,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}]