The upstream issue confirms the true owner is pydantic-core’s shared fields serializer, but this task explicitly constrains the fix to `pydantic/main.py`. I’ll therefore add a narrow Python-side serialization shadow: only when a collision exists, shallow-copy the affected model graph and remove colliding extras before invoking the existing core serializer. This preserves the normal fast path, avoids mutating live models, and covers nested models for both Python and JSON output.
